        <body>
            <div xml:id="d706">

                <pb facs="0643" n="527" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg527"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.111/50.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1012.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 16, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reference to my No. 989 of December 19,
                    1911, I have the honor to enclose herewith copies of further correspondence with
                    the Haitian Government relative to the refusal of licenses to certain American
                    firms.</p>
                <p>There is also enclosed copy and translation of a note on the same subject which,
                    under date of January 3, 1912, was sent to the Haitian Government by the
                    representatives of Great Britain, France, Cuba, Santo Domingo, Austria and
                    Italy.</p>
                <p>I delayed sending my note until the 8th in the hopes that the mail from the
                    States arriving on the 7th would bring me definite instructions from the
                    Department.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">H. W. Furniss.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d706-a1.xml" xpointer="d706-a1"/>
